# Deliberate historical mentions of removed ontology names.
# Entries are either `name` or `path:name`; blank lines and # comments are ignored.
#
# Prefer the path-scoped form. A bare name exempts the whole docs tree, which
# silently disarms the guard for any page that later misuses the name.

# `created_at` was an ontology attribute (removed — nothing ever wrote it). It is
# also the timestamp column on most Postgres tables, and DATABASE.md's relational
# section lists those columns. Scoped to that file so an ontology page that
# resurrects the attribute name still fails the guard.
docs/DATABASE.md:created_at
docs/ko/DATABASE.md:created_at
